1	line	Player	Greetings, your majesty.
1	line	King Roald	Yes, citizen. Do you need something?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	I'm looking for a quest!
2	line	Player	I'm looking for a quest!
2	line	King Roald	A quest you say? Hmm... What an odd request to make of the King. It's funny you should mention it though, as there is something you can do for me.
2	line	King Roald	Are you aware of Paterdomus? It's a temple east of here. It stands on the holy River Salve and guards the only passage into the deadly vampyre-infested lands of Morytania.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Yes, I think I've heard of it.
3	line	Player	Yes, I think I've heard of it.
3	line	King Roald	Very good. Well, it has been some days since last I heard from Drezel, the priest who lives there. Be a sport and go check in on the silly old codger for me, would you?
3	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that your combat level is lower than the recommended level of 15.
3	select	Start the Priest in Peril quest?
3	option	Yes.
4	line	Player	Sure. I don't have anything better to do right now.
4	line	King Roald	Many thanks, adventurer! I would have sent one of the squires, but they wanted payment for it!
4	select	Select an option
4	option	Why do you care about Drezel anyway?
5	action	below
4	option	Do I get a reward for this?
5	action	below
4	option	I'll get going.
5	line	Player	I'll get going.
5	action	end
3	option	No.
4	line	Player	No. That sounds boring.
4	line	King Roald	Yes, I dare say it does. I wouldn't even have mentioned it had you not seemed to be looking for something to do anyway.
4	action	end
1	option	Not really.
1	line	Player	Not really.
2	line	King Roald	You will have to excuse me then. I am very busy as I have a kingdom to run!
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to King Roald again
1	line	Player	Greetings, your majesty.
1	line	King Roald	Yes, citizen. Do you need something?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	About that job I'm doing...
2	line	Player	About that job I'm doing...
2	line	King Roald	You have news of Drezel for me?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Where am I supposed to go again?
3	line	Player	Where am I supposed to go again?
3	line	King Roald	The temple of Paterdomus where Drezel lives. It is but a short journey east from here. It lies at the source of the River Salve. Don't worry, you can't miss it.
3	action	other
2	option	Why do you care about Drezel anyway?
3	line	Player	Why do you care about Drezel anyway?
3	line	King Roald	Well, that is a slightly impertinent question to ask of your King, but I shall overlook it this time.
3	line	King Roald	As you are no doubt aware, this kingdom worships Saradomin, the god of wisdom and order. As such, it is a peaceful place to live and prosper.
3	line	King Roald	Paterdomus, the temple where Drezel lives, stands on the eastern border of Misthalin. It guards the only passage into the evil lands of Morytania.
3	line	Player	Evil?
3	line	King Roald	Oh yes. Morytania is a fearful place, filled to the brim with accursed servants of the chaos god Zamorak. All of them are terrible, but none more so than the rulers of the region, the vampyres.
3	line	King Roald	Thankfully, the sacred River Salve marks a natural border between Misthalin and Morytania. The waters of the river have been blessed with Saradomin's almighty power, preventing any invasion by the vampyres.
3	line	King Roald	Drezel is descended from one of the original Saradominist priests who first blessed the river. His job is to ensure nothing happens to the river that might allow the evil of Morytania to invade this land.
3	line	King Roald	This is the reason why the lack of communication from him bothers me somewhat, although I am sure it's nothing too serious. Nobody would dare to try and attack our kingdom!
3	action	other
2	option	Do I get a reward for this?
3	line	Player	Do I get a reward for this?
3	line	King Roald	You will be rewarded with the knowledge that you have done the right thing and assisted the King of Misthalin.
3	line	Player	So... that would be a 'no' then?
3	line	King Roald	That is correct.
3	action	other
2	option	I have to go.
3	line	Player	I have to go.
3	action	end
1	option	Not really.
2	action	above
