0	section	Saving Drezel and the world
0	section	Attempting to open the coffin on the top floor
1	line	Player	It sounds like there's something alive inside it. I don't think it would be a very good idea to open it...
1	action	end
0	section	Meeting Drezel
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Drezel	Oh! You do not appear to be one of those Zamorakians who imprisoned me! Who are you and why are you here?
1	line	Player	My name's {player}. King Roald sent me to find out what was going on at the temple. I take it you're Drezel?
1	line	Drezel	That's right! Oh, praise be to Saradomin! I feared that when those Zamorakians attacked this place, Misthalin would be doomed!
1	line	Player	Why? What are they planning to do?
1	line	Drezel	I believe they aim to desecrate the blessings placed upon the holy River Salve by the Seven Priestly Warriors themselves! We'd be left defenceless against the vampyres of Morytania!
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Seven Priestly Warriors?
2	line	Player	Seven Priestly Warriors?
2	line	Drezel	Indeed. While this isn't the... ideal time for a history lesson, this knowledge may help you with our next steps, so allow me to explain...
2	line	Drezel	It is said that many years ago, the land that is now Morytania was a peaceful Saradominist kingdom. Alas, all that ended when the vampyres invaded, claiming the land as their own.
2	line	Drezel	Morytania wasn't enough for them though. Soon, they set their sights on these lands as well. Misthalin would have quickly fallen to the vampyres, were it not for the bravery of the Seven Priestly Warriors.
2	line	Drezel	They led the armies of Misthalin against the vampyres, with the war culminating in a great battle that took place right where this temple stands.
2	line	Drezel	For ten days and nights they fought, never sleeping, never eating, fuelled only by their faith in Saradomin.
2	line	Drezel	On the eleventh day, reinforcements arrived, but when they did, they found the Seven Priestly Warriors had been slain by the vampyres, along with most of their forces.
2	line	Drezel	However, their sacrifice was not in vain. Before they were defeated, the Seven Priestly Warriors managed to bless the Salve with the holy power of Saradomin.
2	line	Drezel	Those blessings remain to this day, ensuring no vampyre can cross the river. The temple here was built soon after. It guards the source of the River Salve, and acts as the only passage into Morytania.
2	line	Player	And what about the mausoleum below?
2	line	Drezel	That is the most important part of the temple, for it is where the passage into Morytania is found. It is also the final resting place of the Seven Priestly Warriors.
2	line	Drezel	Their tombs are built around the well that provides direct access to the source of the Salve, with a golden gift placed upon each of the tombs as a mark of respect.
2	line	Player	I see. And you think those Zamorakians are going to try and remove the blessings on the river?
2	line	Drezel	I fear that is almost certainly their goal.
2	line	Player	So what do we do?
2	line	Drezel	First, we need to get me out of this cell. The leader of those Zamorakians probably has the key. I believe he's the one in the hood.
2	line	Player	So I need to go and find this key. Anything else I should be aware of?
2	line	Drezel	I'm afraid so. When the Salve was first blessed, a small number of vampyres were left trapped on this side of it. They were heavily weakened, but still posed a dangerous threat.
2	line	Drezel	Even with them weakened, the brave Saradominists who built this temple were unable to kill them. Instead, they trapped them in coffins and buried them outside the temple.
2	line	Drezel	This coffin here contains one of those vampyres. The Zamorakians must have dug it up and brought it in here with them.
2	line	Player	But why?
2	line	Drezel	Well, as those fiends pointed out to me with delight, as I am the descendant of one of the Seven Priestly Warriors who blessed the river, it will likely recognise the smell of my blood.
2	line	Drezel	If I get too close, it will probably wake up and kill me, very slowly and painfully.
2	line	Player	Maybe I could kill it somehow?
2	line	Drezel	I would not risk waking it. Even now, it could pose a huge threat. The priests of old would incapacitate trapped vampyres with the blessings of Saradomin. Perhaps there's a way for you do the same.
2	line	Player	Right. So, I need to find the key to your cell and do something about the vampyre. Got it.
2	line	Drezel	Good luck.
1	option	What do we do?
2	action	Continues above from "So what do we do?"
