0	section	Attempting to pass the holy barrier before securing the barrier
1	line	Drezel	Stop!
1	line	Player	Can't I go through there?
1	line	Drezel	No, you cannot! It is taking all of my willpower to hold that barrier in place. You must restore the sanctity of the Salve as soon as possible!
1	action	end
0	section	Repairing the barrier
1	line	Drezel	Ah, {player}. Glad you made it. Things are worse than I feared down here. I'm not sure if I will be able to repair the damage.
1	line	Player	How bad is it?
1	line	Drezel	From what I can tell, those Zamorakians used some kind of potion to pollute the Salve. With this being the source, it has already started to spread down the river.
1	line	Drezel	Before long, the blessings placed upon the river will be irreversably damaged. There will be nothing to stop the vampyres from invading Misthalin at their leisure.
1	line	Player	Could you not bless the river like you did with that water earlier?
1	line	Drezel	I'm afraid not. Blessing a small bucket is one thing, but the power I have from Saradomin is nowhere near enough to cleanse an entire river.
1	line	Drezel	However, I believe there might still be a way to undo this, but I'm going to need your help. This passage is the only route between Morytania and Misthalin. The barrier here draws power from the river.
1	line	Drezel	I have managed to reinforce the barrier, but I must continue focussing on it to keep it intact. While I do that, I will need you to soak up the evil magic that potion has released into the river.
1	line	Player	Soak up the magic? How?
1	line	Drezel	I'm sure you know of runes, used by mages to power their spells. The essence used to create them absorbs magical potential from runic altars to be released later.
1	line	Player	Ah, I see where this is going. You think we can use some rune essence to absorb the magic that potion released into the Salve?
1	line	Drezel	Exactly. If you could bring me fifty essence, I should be able to reverse the damage done. Be quick though. The longer we wait, the worse things will get.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Drezel again
1	line	Player	What am I supposed to do again?
1	line	Drezel	Bring me fifty rune essence so that I can undo the damage done by those Zamorakians.
1	action	end
0	section	Bringing Drezel essence
1	line	Player	I brought you some rune essence.
1	line	Drezel	Quickly, give them to me!
1	box	You give Drezel some essence.
1	line	Drezel	Thank you. I need [1-50] more.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Drezel again
1	line	Player	How much more essence do I need to bring you?
1	line	Drezel	I need [1-50] more.
1	action	end
0	section	Bringing Drezel noted essence
1	line	Player	I brought you some rune essence.
1	line	Drezel	You have brought me notes saying 'I promise to pay the bearer on demand the listed number of Rune Essence.' How is that supposed to help me?
1	action	end
0	section	Giving Drezel the last of the essence
1	line	Player	I brought you some more essence.
1	line	Drezel	Quickly, give them to me!
1	box	You give Drezel some essence.
1	line	Drezel	Excellent! That should do it! I will bless these stones and place them within the well so they can soak up the magic from that potion. Misthalin will be safe from the vampyres once more!
1	line	Player	What about the Zamorakians upstairs?
1	line	Drezel	They hopefully shouldn't be too much trouble now that their leader is dead, but I will write to the King and ask him to make sure they're dealt with properly.
1	line	Drezel	For now though, please take this dagger. It has been handed down within my family for generations and is filled with the power of Saradomin. Consider it a small thank you for your help here.
1	line	Player	So can I pass through that barrier now?
1	line	Drezel	Into Morytania? Yes, you can. The barrier will prevent the servants of Zamorak from entering Misthalin, but it is safe for those blessed by Saradomin.
1	line	Drezel	I must warn you though, Morytania is an evil land. The region is filled with creatures and monsters more terrifying than any you'll find on this side of the Salve.
1	line	Drezel	Worst of all are the vampyres, the rulers of Morytania. Be very cautious of their kind. Many are completely immune to human weaponry. Those that aren't, are still very hard to kill.
1	line	Player	I'll be careful. Anything else I should know?
1	line	Drezel	The first settlement you'll likely come across is Canifis, a town of werewolves. They probably won't attack you unless provoked, but you should still be cautious.
1	line	Drezel	You should keep that dagger I gave you to hand. Its magic will prevent them from taking on their wolf form.
1	line	Player	I see. Thanks.
1	line	Drezel	One last thing. While in Morytania, stay alert for any mention of the Myreque.
1	line	Player	The Myreque?
1	line	Drezel	Yes. They're a band of freedom fighters. They fight to protect the humans trapped in Morytania from the tyranny of the vampyres. Their hope is to one day rid the region of all evil.
1	line	Drezel	Veliaf, the leader of their Mort Myre group, is an old friend. I imagine they'd appreciate the help of someone like you, if you can find them.
1	line	Player	I'll keep an eye out for them.
1	line	Drezel	Right, I think that's everything. Just the blessing itself now. Hold still a moment.
1	box	Drezel blesses you, allowing you to pass through the barrier into Morytania.
1	line	Drezel	Good luck out there. Stay safe.
1	option	Do you know of anything I can do in Morytania?
2	action	Continues on Transcript:Drezel
1	option	And you. See you later.
2	line	Player	And you. See you later.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to King Roald
1	line	King Roald	Yes, citizen. Do you need something?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	About that job you gave me...
2	line	Player	About that job you gave me...
2	line	King Roald	Ah, yes, we recieved word from Drezel. I hear the Salve is safe once more. Very good work!
2	line	Player	Thank you. Will you be sending some soldiers over to sort out those Zamorakians?
2	line	King Roald	Yes, yes, we'll make sure they're dealt with. Might take a little while, mind you. Lots of priorities to balance around here. I'm sure we'll have them gone before the end of the year though.
2	line	Player	Right...
2	action	end
1	option	Not really.
2	line	Player	Not really.
2	line	King Roald	You will have to excuse me then. I am very busy as I have a kingdom to run!
2	action	end
